@startuml
title Car Park API - Current Upstream and Proposed Read Contract
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Upstream Car Park API" {
  interface CarParkApi
  class LiveCarParkRecord <<provider payload>> {
    facilityId : provider identifier
    facilityName
    spots
    occupancy
    messageDate : Sydney local wall time (no offset)
  }
  class HistoryQuery {
    facility
    eventdate : YYYY-MM-DD
  }
  CarParkApi --> LiveCarParkRecord : GET /carpark
  CarParkApi --> LiveCarParkRecord : GET /carpark/full-list
  CarParkApi --> HistoryQuery : GET /carpark/history
}

package "This service - proposed read API" {
  class LiveCarParkResponse {
    slug
    facilityName
    spots
    occupancy
    available
    occupancyRate
    availability
    timeMs : epoch milliseconds (UTC instant)
    ariaLabel
  }
  class ParkingHistoryResponse {
    from / to
    resolution
    points : List<HistoryPointTuple>
  }
  enum HistoryResolution {
    TEN_MINUTE
    ONE_HOUR
    SIX_HOUR
    TWELVE_HOUR
    TWENTY_FOUR_HOUR
  }
  class HistoryPointTuple <<JSON tuple>> {
    timeMs : epoch milliseconds
    occupancyRate
    available
  }

  class ParkingController
  class UpstreamCarParkResponseMapper {
    - toInstant(sydneyMessageDate : LocalDateTime) : Instant
  }
  class ApiTimestampMapper {
    + toEpochMillis(instant : Instant) : long
  }
  class OverviewResponseMapper
  class HistoryResponseMapper
  ParkingController --> LiveCarParkResponse : GET /api/v1/parking
  ParkingController --> LiveCarParkResponse : GET /{slug}/overview (or /live)
  ParkingController --> ParkingHistoryResponse : GET /{slug}/history
  OverviewResponseMapper --> ApiTimestampMapper : Instant -> epoch ms
  HistoryResponseMapper --> ApiTimestampMapper : Instant -> epoch ms
  ParkingHistoryResponse o-- "0..*" HistoryPointTuple
  ParkingHistoryResponse --> HistoryResolution
}

note bottom of HistoryPointTuple
  New contract has no legacy-shape requirement. Each compact tuple is
  [timeMs, occupancyRate, available]. The frontend chart uses timeMs and
  occupancyRate; its summary also needs available. Occupancy is omitted.
  AUTO defaults to ten-minute through 1 day, hourly through 7 days, six-hour
  through 14 days, then 24-hour through 31 days. Return actual resolution.
end note

note left of LiveCarParkRecord
  Upstream mapper owns a private conversion helper: interpret
  MessageDate as Australia/Sydney local time, then convert to Instant.
  Do not parse it as UTC: the upstream value has no offset. Persist
  that same instant as BSON UTC date.
  Check the upstream's other time field or define a DST overlap policy:
  an offset-free Sydney wall time can be ambiguous during clock changes.
end note

note right of ApiTimestampMapper
  Shared outbound helper used by response mappers. Convert
  an already-normalized Instant with toEpochMilli(); do not
  apply Sydney timezone conversion a second time.
end note

note right of CarParkApi
  carparkswagger_prod_2.yaml documents /carpark,
  /carpark/full-list, and /carpark/history. Its success
  schemas are opaque `file` types, so the Java provider DTO
  and observed payloads currently supply field-level details.
end note

note right of LiveCarParkResponse
  Current snapshot payload. The /overview to /live path change is optional
  and requires a coordinated frontend route update; the response concept
  can be renamed independently.
end note
@enduml
